{# Department detail widget 'delete' — the one destructive control, with the consequence list
   spelled out ABOVE the button. Design: overview.widgets.js → "delete" (DP·07).
   The consequences are computed from THIS department, not asserted in prose: a reader must be
   able to check the sentence against the record in front of them. Typing the name is the
   confirmation, and the shared confirm-modal controller asks on top of it. #}
<div class="c danger" data-w="delete">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">DP·07</span>Delete this department</span>
    <p class="use">Read this before you click. In plain English, deleting <b>{{ department.name }}</b>
        does exactly this:</p>
    <ul class="conseq">
        <li><b>{{ department.modules|length ? department.modules|map(m => m.name)|join(' and ') ~ ' ' ~ (department.modules|length == 1 ? 'is' : 'are') ~ ' detached.' : 'Nothing is detached.' }}</b>
            The modules, their rows and every number in them stay exactly as they are — any other
            department keeps leading with them.</li>
        <li><b>{{ positions|length ? positions|map(p => p.name)|join(' and ') ~ ' lose their department.' : 'No position is affected.' }}</b>
            The positions survive with the same permissions; they simply sit under no department
            until someone files them again.</li>
        <li><b>The {{ members|length }} {{ members|length == 1 ? 'person keeps' : 'people keep' }} everything.</b>
            Same permissions, same pages, same data — they lose the ordering hint, nothing else.</li>
        <li><b>Its own goals go with it.</b> {{ goals|length }} declared
            {{ goals|length == 1 ? 'goal is' : 'goals are' }} withdrawn. Every module figure they were
            scored from is a module's row and is untouched.</li>
        <li><b>Nothing is deleted anywhere else.</b> A department has never gated data, so removing one
            cannot hide any.</li>
    </ul>
    {% if canManage %}
        <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_department_delete', {uuid: department.uuidString}) }}" class="dp-deleteform">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('department_manage') }}">
            <button class="softbtn danger" type="submit"
                    {{ stimulus_controller('confirm-modal') }}
                    data-action="click->confirm-modal#ask"
                    data-confirm-modal-title-value="Delete “{{ department.name }}”?"
                    data-confirm-modal-message-value="Its modules are detached, its positions lose their department, its people keep every permission they have. Nothing else is deleted."
                    data-confirm-modal-confirm-label-value="Delete department"
                    data-confirm-modal-danger-value="true">{{ ux_icon('lucide:trash-2') }} Delete department</button>
            <span class="fog dp-deletenote">Managers only · not reversible</span>
        </form>
    {% else %}
        <p class="use fog">Managers only.</p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
